From: Uke Linux contributors <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] interconnect: qcom: retain Cliffs NSP and crypto suppliers

Port the exact project supplier identities from 52bbf80 to the signed Linux
7.3 queue. Keep the six existing SH1 display/GPU members and append NSP.
Admit only the exact nsp.lvl ARC resource; no board MMIO or DT enablement is
added. Correct the existing binding metadata to match the native providers.

Compared with Uke OEM kernel 5712080a4b0c0b1a879e6d145c601c649ddaddfd,
OEM DT 94c84aeb9e517dbde546fc732033c184094c8e57 and OnePlus
fc892483f1d61f245924681eb5abd563564d9cba. Retain Qualcomm/Linux GPL
attribution. Host graph checks do not establish physical DSP throughput.

--- a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/qnoc-cliffs-usb.c
+++ b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/qnoc-cliffs-usb.c
@@ -25,11 +25,14 @@
